+    // Reclaim bridge closes that were deferred while the GPU was away. Order matters: this runs after
+    // nv_xnu_pm_open(), so the RM calls a reclaimed close makes count as ordinary callers instead of
+    // being held by the gate this same thread just closed; and it runs on the PM thread, never inside an
+    // NVKMS event callback. When the resume failed (kGpuPmLost) the reclaim attempt fails the same way it
+    // did before, so nothing is reported as closed that is not. A reclaimed client drops the provider
+    // retain it took when it was quarantined, so this service is held across the scan.
+    if (nv_xnu_kms_close_deferred() > 0) {
+        retain();
+        const int deferred = nv_xnu_retry_kms_bridge_closes();
